sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The core equations are implemented in the published form: W_n = exp(-2 n^2 xi^2) - A exp(-2 n^2 xi_hat^2) for the local coupling, the lateral harmonics as the Hankel transform of a normalised Gaussian difference exp(-xi^2 q^2/4) I_n(xi^2 q^2/4) with the anisotropy factor sin(2 n theta_0)/(2 n theta_0) and sign (-1)^n, the dispersion relation lambda_pm(q) = W_1 + beta (W_0 pm W_2) + beta^2 sum_m (W_{m-1} pm W_{m+1})^2/(W_1 - W_m), gamma_3(theta) and eta_hex as orientation integrals of the eigenfunction, the roll criterion 2 gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0, and the exact map x = (alpha/eps) ln(1 + eps r/w_0), y = beta r theta/(w_0 + eps r). Deductions: parity is verified only against the Rust port's own scan values, never against a number, curve or critical wavenumber reported in the paper (-8); branch selection adds a non-paper free-energy \"score\" ranking, a lattice-local fallback, coefficient clipping to +-1.5 and an assumed-stable even hexagon rather than the paper's per-lattice stability analysis (-6); the \"contoured\" planform is rendered as max over phi of a scalar activity then tanh-sharpened, discarding the orientation field that defines contoured planforms in Figs 31-36 (-6); the map constants alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are asserted without derivation (-3); the gallery presets silently inherit lateral_wide_sigma = 1.5 while the Fig 16/17 panel uses 3.0, so the rendered q* = 1.45 is not the q* = 1.0 shown in Panel A (-5). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L389–L438: Local W_n and lateral Fourier-Bessel W_n^lat(q) with sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) anisotropy and normalised-Gaussian 0.5 prefactor; matches Bressloff 2001 Sections 3-4 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L389-L438>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L449–L469: Second-order perturbative dispersion relation lambda_even/odd(q); m=0 term vanishes on the odd branch as in the paper <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L449-L469>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L554–L640: Cubic coefficients and roll criterion 2*gamma3 > gamma0 are correct, but global selection uses an ad-hoc energy score and even-hex stability is assumed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L554-L640>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L837–L850: Contoured rendering collapses the orientation field to max_phi |activity| then tanh(sharpness*.); not the oriented-segment planform of the paper <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L837-L850>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

